  "description": "Timetables on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to e (4608, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e4 d-e, each 1024 long, with dead ends at a and e. Alpha (1536, 512) has a platform along all of e1 and Beta (3584, 512) along all of e4; Gamma (5632, 2560) has none, so no path reaches it. A timetable is a train's ordered list of stops, each a station with a scheduled arrival and departure in game minutes since the start (the clock's scale). setTrainTimetable replaces the whole list and [] clears it; it is free and the train may be unplaced. Times must never go back from minute 0: 0 <= arrival <= departure at every stop, and each departure <= the next arrival; equal times, repeated stations, stations without platforms and times the clock has passed are allowed. Checks, in the order unknownTrain, invalidTimetable, unknownStation (the first missing station in timetable order): new trains have none (also after another train got one), one-stop and multi-stop timetables, zero dwell and equal boundaries, replacing and clearing, rejected commands leave the timetable as it was; the timetable survives place, rate, path, advance, reverse, unplace and a second place, and setting one keeps the train's path (here to 512 along e1, on Alpha's platform) and rate; and it is inert: it never places, moves, routes or stops a train, a train stopped at a scheduled station stays there after its departure time has passed (Local 1 at the end of its path on e1, then placed at d arriving from e on e4, the end of that edge, on Beta's platform), and time passing every scheduled minute leaves the timetable as it was. Balance 1,000,000 less 4 edges of a tile at 1,000, 3 stations at 50,000 and 2 trains at 200,000 (before F3 this ran on five grid track tiles: 445,000).",
